@startuml MES_Order_Status_Write
title MES - Write status change (with cache invalidation)

actor Operator
participant "MES UI (React)" as UI
participant "MES API" as API
database "MES DB (PostgreSQL)" as DB
participant "Redis Cache" as Cache
queue "RabbitMQ" as MQ
participant "CRM API" as CRM

== Operator takes order / changes status ==
Operator -> UI: Click "Take in work"
UI -> API: POST /orders/{order_id}/status {to=MANUFACTURING_STARTED}

API -> DB: BEGIN
API -> DB: UPDATE orders SET status=to, status_changed_at=now() WHERE id=order_id
DB --> API: OK
API -> DB: COMMIT

== Cache invalidation / update ==
API -> Cache: DEL mes:orders:list:FROM:* (first pages)
API -> Cache: DEL mes:orders:list:TO:* (first pages)
API -> Cache: ZREM mes:orders:latest:FROM order_id
API -> Cache: ZADD mes:orders:latest:TO score=now() member=order_id

== Publish event to integration ==
API -> MQ: PUBLISH event(status_changed, order_id, from, to, message_id)
MQ --> CRM: DELIVER event(status_changed)
CRM -> CRM: Update shop/CRM view (if needed)

API --> UI: 200 OK

@enduml
